At last, I tried the game I was interested on and I am humbled for being the betatester of this project (sorry for my english, guys! D: )
I kinda sure this beta was focused in a part of the game and that was not the beginning, I recommend to write this on the disclaimer, otherwise
people might think that was the beginning of the game.
Well, what can we say about the good stuff?
I liked both the music and art, along with the gameplay and battles overall, but I prefer to explain this at the end.
Let's talk about the things to fix, but maybe part of them are already fixed. If yes, good! Less work to do!
I am not perfect, so you will find something to argue about and I have no problem on that, you know. Here's what I found for now:
Spoiler:
Things to fix
- I don't know why, but I get 0 XP from the enemies. During this test, I "cheated" myself some levels when I thought to level up in game.
I beat all the enemies I could anyway and I finished the beta with a level 9. I don't know what was the intended level;
- I prefer an interactive tutorial instead of text on screen. It's a waste losing informations that makes the experience better;
- If you are afraid for people using the DevMenu skill in the game, disable the skill when on battle, so you are 100% testers won't ruin
everything;
- I didn't like the "you can save on this candle because you wanted so" prompt. I don't think it's useful and I will personally remove it;
- I got some "Wrong RID" and "Incorrect Player RID" prompts when I tried to throw a fish in a unintended way. Disable the throwing when it'S
like that;
- I would put in the description of the fish how to use it, since people can forget it;
- You can jump to the fire if you manage to jump to a platform made by a fish and block yourself;
- Some zoom effects are not updated correctly, like going forward and the zoom effect is getting bigger, but it remains as it is when you go back;
- Confidence is a particular mechanic. I would put the exact confidence points Fidel will have in battle instead treating them as normal MPs
outside the battle and then when you enter the battle, the value is changed.
- During the three fish puzzle, you can look freely the map, but if you do, the light applied on the invisible Fidel remains, making this
"Looking Mode"...weird. I would remove the inner light when moving the invisible Fidel when you look at the map;
- The "throwing fish mechanic" must be more intuitive in general. Not only controlling better when the player can throw a fish, but more times
during the game you throw a fish, go to the other side and a platform reappears. It's not intuitive for the player, a better solution might be
throwing a fish on a "weird (desired, intended) spot" and then that platform will stay as it is, it won't go down if you don't jump to the other
side immediately;
- I would adjust the "Engage" menu. Think something for using the extra space left (maybe 4 rows instead 4 columns?) and add a description to
the attack skill, maybe explaining better how it works, like "you can get Confidence points when you attack" or something;
- When you have less confidence than the skill, both Fidel and the enemies can lose a turn doing nothing because they have not enough Confidence
Points. I know this might be tactical (when I had two actions per turn this helped me) like getting hit and having enough points anyway for casting
your spell, but watch out of eventual frustations due to this;
- The names of the enemies aren't understandable enough. They are black and the volcano-like background don't help improving the readingness.
- I can see a "1" on the "Dead" status. It should be removed, unless stacking Dead statuses will have sense in the game, but I don't think so;
- I opened a chest and "Shiny Bubbles" (I think?) was in white...and I had white windows so I didn't understand well. Same with black windows,
you can't see everything else since words are black too;
- I would put a bit more saves. Even with healing torches, saving is not enough present to the game, especially in this game where dungeons
are long.
- When you lose a fight, you can access to the menu. I saw a weird statue class that way;
- I would fix the pre-Caldera Colosso scene. Fidel's bust is not important since it's the same as the portrait, but bigger;
- On Caldera Colosso, you can't do a jump to a platform. Normally you can jump to that platform from the left and the bottom, but the game
makes you jump only from the bottom side;
- There are weird collisions on Caldera-respawnroom;
- At the beginning of Caldera Colosso, the announcer says: "Welcome to Caldera Collosso" instead of "Caldera Colosso";
- You should remove the Lightning Rod mechanic of losing 1 HP each time you recharge it because it doesn't have a utility.
You can't die by recharging too much, you can't risk your life by fighting enemies since they won't do any damage and then
you will be cured before the boss. Also I would remove the error message when you try to recharge a sixth time. Put only the error popup
there;
- You must change the "Caldera-respawnroom" name, since it's visible from the save menù.
...ok, the "must improve" list is finished. I can see great things on this game. It's really ambitious and the premises are there, as I said before I can see this will be a good game. Fix the bugs, improve the tutorial and explainations and let me know when you will have something to test again.

